{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345180",
      "title": "Revisiting Functions & Parameters",
      "sourceHash": "f88a4ac24964a5207278069e1a5e640f238394f8eddaecc5f9c936bf9479a95f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.44,
          "en": "Now, besides the variables and constants,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.44,
          "end": 8.58,
          "en": "an ever crucial JavaScript concept are functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.58,
          "end": 10.74,
          "en": "which can either be created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.74,
          "end": 13.08,
          "en": "with help of the function keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.08,
          "end": 15.78,
          "en": "or with help of this arrow function syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.78,
          "end": 17.88,
          "en": "to which I'll get back in a couple of seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.88,
          "end": 20.07,
          "en": "Let's start with the function keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 22.26,
          "en": "The idea behind functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.26,
          "end": 24.66,
          "en": "no matter how you are creating them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.66,
          "end": 27.03,
          "en": "simply is that you're defining some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.03,
          "end": 29.31,
          "en": "that's not executed immediately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.31,
          "end": 32.07,
          "en": "but instead, at some point in the future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.07,
          "end": 34.05,
          "en": "when you call the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.05,
          "end": 37.14,
          "en": "and that can be executed as often as you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.14,
          "end": 40.14,
          "en": "because a function can be called multiple times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.14,
          "end": 41.22,
          "en": "Now, to show you what I mean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.22,
          "end": 42.93,
          "en": "let me finish this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 42.93,
          "end": 45.81,
          "en": "And this is how you write a basic function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 45.81,
          "end": 49.41,
          "en": "You give it a name which comes after the function keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.41,
          "end": 51.66,
          "en": "Then you have a so-called \"parameter list\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 51.66,
          "end": 53.34,
          "en": "to which I'll get back in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 53.34,
          "end": 56.91,
          "en": "You do create it with a opening and closing parenthesis",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 56.91,
          "end": 59.16,
          "en": "and you need these parenthesis here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 59.16,
          "end": 62.04,
          "en": "and then you have opening and closing curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.04,
          "end": 64.17,
          "en": "And between those curly braces,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 64.17,
          "end": 66.39,
          "en": "you put your function code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 69.06,
          "en": "So, the code that's not executed right now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 69.06,
          "end": 71.28,
          "en": "but at some point in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 71.28,
          "end": 72.69,
          "en": "So, for example, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 72.69,
          "end": 75.48,
          "en": "I could put a console log statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 75.48,
          "end": 76.74,
          "en": "into this greet function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 76.74,
          "end": 80.03999999999999,
          "en": "and if I would save this and reload this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 80.03999999999999,
          "end": 82.86,
          "en": "you would see nothing in the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 82.86,
          "end": 86.03999999999999,
          "en": "The reason for that is that this function is defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 86.03999999999999,
          "end": 87.75,
          "en": "but never executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 87.75,
          "end": 88.89,
          "en": "Because as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 88.89,
          "end": 90.75,
          "en": "with a function, you're defining code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 90.75,
          "end": 93.15,
          "en": "that's not executed immediately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 93.15,
          "end": 97.11,
          "en": "but at some point in the future when you call the function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 97.11,
          "end": 99.66,
          "en": "when you invoke the function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 99.66,
          "end": 103.2,
          "en": "And you do that by using the name of the function like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 103.2,
          "end": 106.86,
          "en": "and then adding another pair of parenthesis after that name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 106.86,
          "end": 109.593,
          "en": "but without the function keyword in front of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 110.46000000000001,
          "end": 112.53,
          "en": "With the function keyword in front of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 112.53,
          "end": 114.3,
          "en": "you're defining it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 114.3,
          "end": 116.07,
          "en": "you are calling it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 116.07,
          "end": 119.88,
          "en": "And now, when this code is encountered in your code file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 119.88,
          "end": 123.3,
          "en": "the code in the function will be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 123.3,
          "end": 125.4,
          "en": "So, now with this added, if I save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 125.4,
          "end": 126.99,
          "en": "and if I reload this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 126.99,
          "end": 129.36,
          "en": "now, I do see \"Hello!\" here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 129.36,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "because now we're calling the function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 132.9,
          "en": "And, as mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 132.9,
          "end": 135.99,
          "en": "I can call the function as often as I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 135.99,
          "end": 140.16,
          "en": "You can literally add as many function invocations here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 140.16,
          "end": 142.74,
          "en": "as needed, and if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 142.74,
          "end": 146.853,
          "en": "you'll therefore see \"Hello!\" being output five times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 148.14,
          "end": 152.07,
          "en": "Because I have five function invocations here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 152.07,
          "end": 155.49,
          "en": "That's how you define and call a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 155.49,
          "end": 157.59,
          "en": "And this is a super important concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 157.59,
          "end": 160.35,
          "en": "which we'll use all the time throughout this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 160.35,
          "end": 163.38,
          "en": "Also, especially, in React, it turns out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 163.38,
          "end": 167.22,
          "en": "that we'll define a crucial React building block",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 167.22,
          "end": 168.32999999999998,
          "en": "as a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 168.32999999999998,
          "end": 170.85,
          "en": "but you'll learn more about this later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 170.85,
          "end": 173.28,
          "en": "once we dive into React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 173.28,
          "end": 176.31,
          "en": "Now, functions cannot just be defined and executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 176.31,
          "end": 177.143,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 177.143,
          "end": 179.73,
          "en": "Instead, they also take so-called \"parameters\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 179.73,
          "end": 181.98,
          "en": "input values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 181.98,
          "end": 185.46,
          "en": "For example, \"username\" and \"message\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 185.46,
          "end": 188.19,
          "en": "You can add as many parameters as you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 188.19,
          "end": 190.68,
          "en": "You simply separate them with a comma.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 190.68,
          "end": 195.06,
          "en": "These parameters are then available inside of the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 195.06,
          "end": 196.89,
          "en": "and only there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 196.89,
          "end": 200.337,
          "en": "So, here I could then output \"username\"-",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 201.63,
          "end": 203.137,
          "en": "Whoops.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 203.137,
          "end": 203.97,
          "en": "With a capital \"N\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 203.97,
          "end": 206.727,
          "en": "And then, thereafter, also \"message\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 208.23,
          "end": 211.38,
          "en": "I can do this because I'm accepting these two parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 211.38,
          "end": 212.85,
          "en": "and since it's your function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 212.85,
          "end": 214.92000000000002,
          "en": "these parameter names are up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 214.92000000000002,
          "end": 217.05,
          "en": "but they have to follow the same rules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 217.05,
          "end": 219.39,
          "en": "as these variable names did.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 219.39,
          "end": 220.35,
          "en": "And the same, by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 220.35,
          "end": 222.27,
          "en": "is also true for the function name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 222.27,
          "end": 224.64,
          "en": "This should also be defined just as you learned it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 224.64,
          "end": 225.9,
          "en": "for the variable names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 225.9,
          "end": 226.733,
          "en": "For example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 226.733,
          "end": 228.84,
          "en": "if it's a word that consists of multiple words,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 228.84,
          "end": 232.17000000000002,
          "en": "you would also use this CamelCase notation here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 232.17000000000002,
          "end": 234.96,
          "en": "So, now this function takes two input parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 234.96,
          "end": 237.48,
          "en": "Therefore, when you are calling this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 237.48,
          "end": 241.98,
          "en": "you also should provide values for these input parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 241.98,
          "end": 242.813,
          "en": "because in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 242.813,
          "end": 244.56,
          "en": "the idea behind using parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 244.56,
          "end": 247.59,
          "en": "simply is that you can have one reusable function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 247.59,
          "end": 251.76,
          "en": "that can be reused with different input values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 251.76,
          "end": 253.29,
          "en": "For example, here, I could call it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 253.29,
          "end": 257.238,
          "en": "with \"Max\" and \"Hello!\" the first time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 257.238,
          "end": 260.44,
          "en": "and then call it again where I greet Manuel",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 261.339,
          "end": 265.71,
          "en": "and say, \"Hello, what's up?\" like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 265.71,
          "end": 267.3,
          "en": "Now, I'm using the same function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 267.3,
          "end": 269.28,
          "en": "with different input values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 269.28,
          "end": 271.32,
          "en": "That's possible, thanks to parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 271.32,
          "end": 273.42,
          "en": "and therefore, If I reload this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 273.42,
          "end": 276.03,
          "en": "I see \"Max\" and \"Hello!\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 276.03,
          "end": 278.997,
          "en": "and then I see \"Manuel\" and \"Hello, what's up?\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 280.14,
          "end": 281.97,
          "en": "Now, what's also worth noting here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 281.97,
          "end": 286.08,
          "en": "is that you can also assign default values to parameters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 286.08,
          "end": 287.79,
          "en": "by adding an equal sign here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 287.79,
          "end": 289.467,
          "en": "For example, \"Hello!\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 290.37,
          "end": 293.55,
          "en": "This would allow me to call this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 293.55,
          "end": 296.82,
          "en": "without providing a value for the second parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 296.82,
          "end": 298.26,
          "en": "And if I don't provide one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 298.26,
          "end": 301.02,
          "en": "the default value will be used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 301.02,
          "end": 304.56,
          "en": "But I can, of course, also override that default value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 304.56,
          "end": 307.923,
          "en": "by simply providing a value for that parameter here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 309.06,
          "end": 310.737,
          "en": "With that, if we reload this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 310.737,
          "end": 314.68,
          "en": "I get \"Max\" and \"Hello!\" thanks to this default here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 315.84,
          "end": 318.33,
          "en": "and then I get \"Manuel\" and \"Hello, what's up?\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 318.33,
          "end": 322.263,
          "en": "where I do use this value for overriding the default.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 323.58,
          "end": 326.46,
          "en": "Now, functions cannot just take input values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 326.46,
          "end": 328.77,
          "en": "but they can also return values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 328.77,
          "end": 330.33299999999997,
          "en": "by using the \"return\" keyword.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 331.29,
          "end": 333.03,
          "en": "So, for example, in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 333.03,
          "end": 335.97,
          "en": "instead of console log in username and message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 335.97,
          "end": 338.85,
          "en": "I could return a string that combines both.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 338.85,
          "end": 340.53,
          "en": "I could return a string here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 340.53,
          "end": 345.3,
          "en": "where I say, \"Hi I am\", a white space here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 345.3,
          "end": 347.64,
          "en": "and then I add the \"userName\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 347.64,
          "end": 351.789,
          "en": "and then another white space or dot maybe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 351.789,
          "end": 353.703,
          "en": "and then the message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 355.40999999999997,
          "end": 357.65999999999997,
          "en": "So, now with that, I'm using this function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 357.65999999999997,
          "end": 359.64,
          "en": "to, in the end, construct a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
